  "answer": "a = 1, b = -1",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Divisibility ignores signs.",
    "Try a number and its negative."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Take $a = 1$, $b = -1$: $1 \\mid -1$ and $-1 \\mid 1$, but $1 \\ne -1$.",
    "So the statement is false. (It is true for natural numbers.)"
  ],
